### Create a new teacher
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/register/teacher
Content-Type: application/json

{
  \"name\": \"teacher2\",
  \"email\": \"profmath@gmail.com\",
  \"password\": \"prof1234\",
  \"confirmPassword\": \"prof1234\",
  \"teacherSubjectId\" : 6
}

### Login with teacher2 (egnoring enabled field for now)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  \"email\": \"profdemath@gmail.com\",
  \"password\": \"prof1234\"
 
}

### Create a new student
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/register/student
Content-Type: application/json

{
  \"name\": \"techstd\",
  \"email\": \"sttechi@gmail.com\",
  \"password\": \"student202\",
  \"confirmPassword\": \"student202\",
  \"studentLevel\": \"HIGH_SCHOOL\",
  \"yearId\": 7,
  \"streamTypeId\": 3,
  \"substreamId\": 20
}

### Global search (teachers by name, courses by title/description, lessons by title/content)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/search?q=math&limit=20

### Published course by id (for \"view course\" from search)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/courses/1

### Progress — dashboard stats (lessons completed, enrollments count, student points)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/me/stats?studentId=1

### Progress — mark lesson complete
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/lessons/1/complete?studentId=1

### Progress — course % and global %
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/courses/1/progress?studentId=1
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/students/1/progress

### Continue learning (optional courseId)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/continue-learning?studentId=1
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/continue-learning?studentId=1&courseId=1

### Test Lessons endpoint (filter nulls fix)
### GET course lessons (e.g. course 2 from task)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/courses/{{courseId}}/lessons
### Example: 
# GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/courses/2/lessons

### TEST UPDATE LESSON (400 fix)
### PUT course lesson - minimal (no resource)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/courses/3/lessons/24
Content-Type: application/json

{
  \"title\": \"Updated Lesson Title Test\",
  \"content\": \"Updated content test - no resource\"
}

### PUT with resource update
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/courses/3/lessons/24
Content-Type: application/json

{
  \"title\": \"Updated with video\",
  \"content\": \"Test\",
  \"resource\": {
    \"videoUrl\": \"https://example.com/video.mp4\",
    \"pdfUrl\": \"\"
  }
}

### PUT with empty resource (should skip, no error)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/courses/3/lessons/24
Content-Type: application/json

{
  \"title\": \"Test empty resource\",
  \"resource\": {
    \"videoUrl\": \"\",
    \"pdfUrl\": \"\"
  }
}

